# GNAT / Alire / SPARK compiler artifacts
# These were previously untracked-but-not-ignored, which left ~1000 generated
# files in `git status`. All of them are fully regenerable from source.
*.ali
*.glob
*.aux
*.vo
*.vok
*.vos
*.nra
.nra.cache
*.cache

# Auto-generated Coq/WhyML obligation stubs emitted by the verifier pipeline.
# These files literally declare themselves "UNPROVED - obligation stub" and
# contain syntactically invalid WhyML, so committing them would misrepresent
# them as real proofs.
#
# The generated stubs are named after whatever Ada unit they came from
# (Test_*, Earu_*, Sabotage_verifier_*, Print_offsets_*, Realtime_helper_*, ...),
# so prefix matching is unmaintainable. The reliable discriminator is the
# hand-authored naming convention instead: a real proof is named
# "<unit>_proof.v" (earu-watchdog_a_proof.v, test_gravity_nav_proof.v, ...).
# The PROOF_MISSING audit rule also expects real proofs by that exact name.
EARU_daemon/src/proofs/*
!EARU_daemon/src/proofs/*_proof.v

# Verifier / link caches and local runtime state
.verifier_cache/
.link_verification_cache.json
.bt_hash
.tmp/
.earu_ramdisk_dev

# PAR2 parity-recovery state written by the self-patching parity engine.
# Machine-specific and regenerable: each .par2 embeds an absolute source_path
# and a source_hash, so it is meaningless on any other checkout.
.parity/

# Stray nested path artifact: EARU_daemon/src/src/utils/sabotage_verifier.py is
# a byte-identical duplicate of the tracked ./src/utils/sabotage_verifier.py,
# created by running a path command from inside EARU_daemon/src/.
EARU_daemon/src/src/
